Run these on the Linux machine:
ls -l /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/

You should see something like:
r22-flight-school.crt

Then verify that file is a valid single certificate:
openssl x509 \
  -in /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/r22-flight-school.crt \
  -noout -subject -issuer -dates

You should get output similar to:
subject=CN = R22 Flight School Local CA
issuer=CN = R22 Flight School Local CA
notBefore=...
notAfter=...

If that works, rebuild the trust store:
sudo update-ca-certificates --fresh

Then verify Linux actually installed it:
ls -l /etc/ssl/certs | grep -i r22



systemctl --user stop r22-flight-school.service 2>/dev/null || true

sudo fuser -k 8086/tcp 2>/dev/null || true

rm -f data/server.pid

./deploy/start_linux.sh
